Currently I use ansible.builtin.unarchive to download tarballs and zip files from a webserver. Unfortunately I'm unable
to change the location where it initially downloads the archive to and it chooses a path beneath the users home directory.

I would like to build a module utility under the collection namespace wtferris to replace this functionality.
These are the features I would like to include:

* This has to support python 2.4 and greater
* I would like to avoid external python dependencies
* Inputs:
  * installation path
  * temporary directory root path (default to installation path)
  * source url for the archive (can be local or remote, eg: file://, http://, or https://)
  * flag for insecure connections if https is choosen
  * a flag to skip post relocation
  * and md5sum value
  * package inventory directory (defaulted to ~/.package_installation)
  * a flag to force installation
* The source archive can either be a gzip tar (file extentension is .tgz or .tar.gz) or a zip (file extension is .zip)
* I would prefer to use the gzip, tar, and unzip utilities budled with the os to unpack the archive
* I would like to create a temporary directory (using mtktemp) in the temporary directory root path. (Referd to tempdir
  going forward)
* A directory should be created underneath the tempdir named extract where the archive will be unpacked
* If possible, I would like to stream the download directly into gzip/tar to exgtract it (this is not necessary for zip files
  unless it can be done in a portable manner - primarily this will be used on Redhat variants 7.x and greater, it could
  be useful for solaris 5.10 and greater tho)
* While downloading, I would like to generate the md5sum value to optionally compare against the md5sum input value
* If a failure is detected, or the md5sum doesn't match the input, the temporary directory and contents should be cleaned up
  and an error should be raised
* Once extracted, there should be only a single directory inside extract folder. If no errors are detected then the
  directory should be moved to the installation directory and a symlink should be create in the package inventory with the
  name .{md5sum value}.md5 which points to the directory that was moved to the installation directoy
* It should be idempotent. If the input md5sum is found in the package inventory and the directory that it points to exists,
  then assume the archive has been installed. Or if the extracted directory exists beneath the installation directory, also assume
  the package was already installed. 

I would like the utility to both be exposed to use in playbooks directly, but also by additional modules. The output should
return the md5sum, a flag that it failed or not, any errors, the directory that was installed if the post install wasn't skipped,
or the tempdir if post install was skipped.



Could you change a few things:

If package.tar.gz contains the directory linux-x64-blah, I would like the entire path to this directory return, eg: /u01/software/linux-x64-blah.
Lastly, I think tempdir should always be returned even if the post relocation step is skipped.
